  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sameer Jaysingh Kanchan vs The State Of Maharashtra on 16 April, 2024 Author: Sarang V. Kotwal Bench: Sarang V. Kotwal 2024:Bhc-As:17704 5-A In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1018 Of 2024 Yugandhara Sameer Jaysingh Kanchan .... Applic Sharad Patil Digitally signed by Versus Yugandhara Sharad Patil Date: 2024.04.17 16:44:42 +0530 The State of Maharashtra .... Respond ______ Mr. Rajesh More , for the applicant. Ms. Poonam P. Bhosale , App for the State/Respondent. _ _ ____ Coram :Sarang V. Kotwal, J. Date : 16th April, 2024 P.C. : 1. The Applicant is seeking anticipatory bail in connection with C.R No.103 of 2024, registered at Uruli Kanchan Police Station, Pune, on 25/03/2024, under Sections 328, 188, 269, 273 of the Indian Penal Code and under Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(d), 27 (3)(e) and 59(iii) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Sameer Jaysingh Kanchan vs The State Of Maharashtra on 16 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/142641549/ 1",
    "facts": "Therefore, the custodial interrogation of the y.s.patil 2 of 4 5-ABA-1018-2024.odt Applicant is not necessary.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the Applicant submitted that offence under section 328 of the I.P.C. is not made out. The issue is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. The contraband is already seized."
  },
